From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AdrielOrihuela <adriel.orihuela.m@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 07:54:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Block for (1 + damage) * 0.5 as 1.8 did

Blocking cannot be expressed as a multiplier: 1.8's formula depends on the
damage, so a hit of seven blocks down to four rather than three and a half,
and a hit of one is not reduced at all. Treating it as a plain halving made
blocking look stronger than it was against big hits and weaker against small
ones.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/entity/LivingEntity.java b/net/minecraft/world/entity/LivingEntity.java
index a1c18b5af8ce896883ffd8cce5868ce2079d082d..eacb9df6491ede267e80c194806375edf9f7cb9d 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/entity/LivingEntity.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/entity/LivingEntity.java
@@ -1491,12 +1491,13 @@ public abstract class LivingEntity extends Entity implements Attackable, Waypoin
             damage = Float.MAX_VALUE;
         }
 
-        // LegacyFolia start - a raised sword halves the hit, as in 1.8
+        // LegacyFolia start - a raised sword takes (1 + damage) * 0.5, as in 1.8
         // Applied here rather than through the BLOCKS_ATTACKS component, because swords do not
         // carry one and giving them a synthetic one would change what every other part of the
-        // game believes a sword is.
-        damage *= io.github.adrielorihuela.legacyfolia.combat.Combat.blockingMultiplier(this);
-        // LegacyFolia end - a raised sword halves the hit
+        // game believes a sword is. This sits before the armour step because 1.8 ran blocking
+        // first, so the two compound.
+        damage = io.github.adrielorihuela.legacyfolia.combat.Combat.afterBlocking(this, damage);
+        // LegacyFolia end - a raised sword takes (1 + damage) * 0.5
 
         EntityDamageEvent event; // CraftBukkit // Paper - move this into the actual invuln check....
         boolean tookFullDamage = true;
